@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+# Task: Host card facts, our own INDUS AGENT banner, curator card check (W59-K2) Phase: ui-parity Owner: builder w59k2
+
+Status: Built (2026-10-25, wave 59 builder K2, base main 65120c2). Uncommitted, for the integrator.
+
+Read: the wave 59 and wave 54 briefs, the second compare's gap list (web system, chat,
+chat-sidebar-closed lines), the reference and Indus captures `system--{light,dark}.png` and
+`chat--dark.png` (looked at for layout only: which facts the Host card lists, that the chat banner
+is large art over a facts/tools box). Our own sources: `src/indus/web/routes/{system,learning}.py`,
+`src/indus/service/{session_header,picker_reads}.py`, `src/indus/protocol/events.py`
+(`SessionInfo`), `apps/web/src/pages/system/MachineSections.tsx`, `apps/tui/src/components/
+{MessageRow,Transcript}.tsx`, `apps/tui/src/app/{App,appRuntime}.tsx`, `apps/tui/e2e/demo2.e2e.test.ts`.
+No reference code, art or assets opened. Evidence ids: none.
+
+What it does (own words):
+
+- Host facts. `GET /api/system/stats` also answers `os` ("Linux 6.1.0": OS name and kernel
+  release), `arch` (machine architecture), `python` ("CPython 3.13.2") and `uptime_seconds` (host
+  uptime from `psutil.boot_time()` when psutil is there, else `/proc/uptime`; null when neither
+  says). Read-only, no host name, user name or path. The web Host card shows OS, Arch and Python
+  first, then Indus, CPU, Memory, Disk, Uptime ("1h 21m", "3d 4h", "<1m") and Load avg; a fact
+  the server does not send (older server) or sends as null has no tile.
+- TUI banner. Our own five-row "INDUS AGENT" in double-line box strokes (letters designed here:
+  I N D U S A G E T), INDUS in the accent tone and AGENT in the text tone, one line wide (59
+  cells). Under it a rounded box: from 90 columns the session facts (model · provider, folder,
+  title, session) on the left and on the right "Tools (N)" with the tool names `session.info`
+  sends (four lines, then "… and N more"), "Skills (N)" and "N tools · N skills · /help for
+  commands"; from 44 columns the same stacked in one column (three lines of names); below 44 the
+  old plain label list. The art degrades to the old three-row wordmark below 60 columns and to the
+  plain name below 32. The skills count is the number of `kind: "skill"` entries in the
+  `commands.catalog` reply the TUI already loads (`uiStore.skillCount`, null until it loads, and
+  then the Skills line is left out).
+- Goldens. The demo e2e masks the tool-name lines (they change whenever a tool is added) and the
+  counts; goldens re-recorded with `INDUS_E2E_UPDATE=1` and reviewed.
+- Skill curator card: not added. No web or gateway route exposes the curator's state; it is
+  only reachable through `indus curator status` and the `/curator` slash command. A card would
+  need a new read route over `learning.curator.state`, which this wave does not invent.
+
+Decisions: W59-K2-1 the stats route carries `os`, `arch`, `python`, `uptime_seconds` (host uptime,
+not process uptime), never a host name. W59-K2-2 the banner art is our own double-line letter set;
+width tiers 60 / 32 for the art, 90 / 44 for the box. W59-K2-3 the skills count comes from the
+catalogue's skill entries (slash-invocable skills), not a new request. W59-K2-4 no Skill curator
+card on the web System page: the backend serves no curator status to the web.
+
+Follow-ups: a read-only `GET /api/learning/curator` (state, interval, last run, paused) would let
+the web System page and the desktop command centre show the curator card the reference has; the
+banner could group tools by toolset if `session.info` sent the toolset of each tool.
+
+Compare checklist:
+- [x] Written from our own sources; no reference code, CSS, art or assets; banner letters ours.
+- [x] Only data our backend already serves, plus four read-only host facts on an existing route.
+- [x] Narrow terminals degrade (art tiers and box tiers), never wider than the terminal (tested).
+- [x] Goldens updated deliberately; tool names and counts masked.
